Description:
Company: CyberLens Ltd (www.cyberlens.eu)
Location: London
Post Type: In-house consultant - Full Time
Duration: 1 year with the possibility of an extension
Beginning: September 1, 2020
CyberLens is specialized in cyber security and privacy technologies, with a particular emphasis on Internet of Things (IoT), 5G, artificial intelligence and other data-driven technologies. Our company has been recently awarded with a number of large EU research and innovation grants. As part of the continuous growth and expansion in our activities, we are looking to hire hard-working and enthusiastic individuals to join our research and innovation team. The successful candidate will gain exceptional experience in the planning and delivery of large-scale research and innovation projects at the forefront of technology and will collaborate with some of the biggest names in the industry. Indicative partners of ours in current large-scale projects include, among others; Ericsson, Deutsche Telekom, Nokia, Qualcomm, BMW, FIAT, ATOS, Thales,
Job Description
We are looking to hire a Machine Learning Engineer to join the Cybersecurity Product Development team. You will play a critical role by engineering cybersecurity products and services with a truly global impact. The most essential duties associated with this position are as follows:
Core responsibility : The candidate will be developing and Implementing machine learning / deep learning algorithms to solve cyber security-related use cases and help engineer products That defend the system against attackers;
Engineer : The candidate should be an engineer at heart, possessing software engineering skills that allow them to build and engineer new ML/DL capabilities vs. simply integrating existing open source components ;
ML / DL skillset: The candidate will be Utilizing information retrieval, data analytics and statistical modeling techniques to build new machine learning and deep learning models. This will include the entire life-cycle including a collection of data, feature engineering, model development, training, testing, and deployment into production;
R&D: Develop prototypes and algorithms (eg searching, sorting, optimization, dynamic programming) while performing engineering tasks around data aggregation and synthesis data from a multitude of structured and unstructured data sources;
Plan and estimate yours and team's work based on features, stories and tasks in the product backlog;
Design, develop, review and test changes in the product according to use cases and requirements.
Skillset
Essential skills:
Software Engineering: The candidate must have a background in software engineering, object-oriented programming languages like Python, C ++;
Machine Learning Concepts: knowledge and experience working with unsupervised and supervised machine learning techniques and algorithms, including but not limited to clustering, outlier detection, single and multiclass classification, autoencoders and sequence-based deep neural networks (e.g., LSTM, Transformer Models). Knowledge and experience with online learning and feature engineering for time series data;
Machine Learning Frameworks: knowledge of common ML frameworks and libraries Keras, PyTorch, TensorFlow, sci-kit-learn;
Solid software engineering knowledge: Agile, Scrum, UML, OOP, design patterns, Multi-Threaded'
Experience with automated unit / regression testing;
Experience in managing full-life development cycles;
Team player with excellent communication skills;
Analytical thinking and pragmatic problem-solving capability;
Able to communicate clearly, work independently and manage time.
Desirable skills:
Knowledge/understanding of Reinforcement Learning techniques and algorithms;
Knowledge of OS coding techniques, IP protocols, interfaces and hardware subsystems;
Understanding of computer network communication principles;
Understanding in development of Anomaly / Intrusion Detection Systems.
Offer
Depending on your knowledge and experience, a gross fee indication between £ 45,000 - £ 53,000 annually on the basis of a 40-hour working week;
A professional, high-tech working environment;
Opportunity to grow in a rapidly growing start-up.
Job Types: Full-time, Contract
Salary: £45,000.00 - £53,000.00 per year
Work remotely:
No

Our business
J.P. Morgan Global Credit Trading business is a global leading market maker in bonds, credit derivatives, exotic products and solutions. It offers first-class, highly integrated financial services to a global client base and provides financial assets and liquidity for banks, insurance companies, finance companies, mutual funds and hedge funds. Traders, salespeople and research analysts work collectively to generate ideas and provide markets to clients.
Our team
The Credit Systematic Market Making is part of the EMEA Credit Trading and performs end-to-end systematic trading of credit products, including Corporate and Emerging Market Bonds. We apply a scientific approach to trading by combining an understanding of market microstructure with modern data analytics to develop quoting, market-making and hedging strategies.
The candidate will be part of Quantitative Research, which is responsible for providing quantitative analytics and models to facilitate and optimize trading and risk management in the global CIB Markets Business. The responsibilities of the team span the full range from new model specification, research and implementation, applying for model approval, to integration into production systems as well as their day-to-day support.
Opportunity
This exciting opportunity is at the intersection of trading, data science and quantitative research. The candidate would join our Credit Systematic Market Making team in London as an Associate or Vice President, working as part of the Credit Trading desk to shape the future of the bond portfolio trading business. This is a unique opportunity to combine state-of-the-art machine learning skills with systematic trading and risk management.
Responsibilities
Development, deployment and support of algorithms and tools for real-time pricing of corporate bonds;
Applying machine learning and statistical techniques to EMEA bond markets;
Conduct research and statistical analysis to build and refine monetization systems for trading signals, including alpha signals, hedging strategies and liquidation strategies;
Written and verbal communication with Model Review Groups in order to make models pass strict in-house standards.

Requirements:
We work in a very dynamic environment. Excellent communication skills are required in our interaction with trading, technology, and control functions. The role requires a commercial mindset. A healthy interest in good software design principles is important. Prior experience working in a data driven research environment is an absolute requirement; a Ph.D. in a machine learning subject or related quantitative field from a top academic institution is a plus.
Essential skills:

Familiarity with fixed income analytics such as curve building and spread analytics;
Strong data science background, including statistics, probability and machine learning; familiarity with concepts as parameter optimization, regularization, neural networks or Gaussian processes;
Excellent practical data analytics skills on real data sets, including familiarity with methods for working with large data and tools for data analysis (pandas, numpy, scikit, TensorFlow);
Good programming and OO design skills. Java and Python will be a plus, as would experience with reactive programming and a strong understanding of scripting languages;
Good understanding of numerical algorithms and data structures;
Attention to detail: thorough and persistent in delivering production quality analytics;
Ability to work in a high-pressure environment;
Pro-active attitude: a self-learner, the candidate should be passionate about problem solving and should have a natural interest to learn about our business, models and infrastructure.
J.P. Morgan is a global leader in financial services, providing strategic advice and products to the world's most prominent corporations, governments, wealthy individuals and institutional investors. Our first-class business in a first-class way approach to serving clients drives everything we do. We strive to build trusted, long-term partnerships to help our clients achieve their business objectives.
We recognize that our people are our strength and the diverse talents they bring to our global workforce are directly linked to our success. We are an equal opportunity employer and place a high value on diversity and inclusion at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of any protected attribute, including race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital or veteran status, pregnancy or disability, or any other basis protected under applicable law. In accordance with applicable law, we make reasonable accommodations for applicants' and employees' religious practices and beliefs, as well as any mental health or physical disability needs.

Opportunity
We're seeking a person to join a team within Rates Quantitative Research working on some important and relatively unexplored topics: structured repos, inflation exotics, bespoke bond derivatives, pricing of less-liquid securities, relative value, collateral optimisation, pricing and risk management tools for repo and bond traders.
We expect the person to share in a balanced mixture of responsibilities, including support for and discussions with traders, model research and development, model documentation, pricing and risk investigation, product-specific analysis, software and trading tool development.
Responsibilities
Develop models and implement them in Python/C++ for pricing and risk managing trades;
Rapidly build prototype models and tools; compare results of various techniques;
Explain model behavior and predictions to traders and controllers, identify major sources of risk in portfolios, carry out scenario analysis, provide guidance/debug analytics;
Write well-formulated documents of model specification and implementation testing.

Essential skills, experience and qualifications
Strong software development and Python/C++ skills;
Strong analytical and problem solving abilities;
Familiarity with probability theory, stochastic processes, and numerical analysis;
Good communication skills, both oral and written;
PhD or equivalent in Mathematics, Math Finance, Physics, or other quantitative subject.

Desirable
Knowledge of financial products, from loans, repos and bonds to structured and exotic deals;
knowledge of machine learning/statistical techniques.
J.P. Morgan is a global leader in financial services, providing strategic advice and products to the world's most prominent corporations, governments, wealthy individuals and institutional investors. Our first-class business in a first-class way approach to serving clients drives everything we do. We strive to build trusted, long-term partnerships to help our clients achieve their business objectives.
We recognize that our people are our strength and the diverse talents they bring to our global workforce are directly linked to our success. We are an equal opportunity employer and place a high value on diversity and inclusion at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of any protected attribute, including race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital or veteran status, pregnancy or disability, or any other basis protected under applicable law. In accordance with applicable law, we make reasonable accommodations for applicants' and employees' religious practices and beliefs, as well as any mental health or physical disability needs.

We’re looking for a Data Scientist with good foundations in a wide range of programming, mathematical, statistical and data science techniques. The ideal candidate will be happy working alone but will still be a team player who can confidently and proactively communicate across the organisation.

Responsibilities
Help us expand our existing reporting and dashboard solutions.
Design and perform statistical analysis which will help us understand our userbase better and which will support our A/B Testing needs.
Run ad-hoc queries against our data warehouse.
Work closely with various technical and non-technical business areas and make sure that strategic decisions are backed by the available data.


Requirements
Advanced SQL (common table extensions, window functions etc.) - any flavour will do;
Good knowledge of of the Python data analysis toolkit (jupyter notebooks, numpy, pandas, matplotlib, plotly etc.). Knowledge of R / SaS / Stata will also be considered;
Solid understanding of basic statistics fundamentals and applications (such as designing and interpreting A/B tests, cohort analysis, t-tests, z-tests, hypothesis etc.);
Any experience with BI tools like Mode Analytics/Tableau/Looker and web analytics platforms like Mixpanel and Keen Io;
Ability to quickly learn new concepts and apply them.
Bonus Skills
Hands-on experience with cloud platform solutions like Google Cloud Platform (Compute Engine, BigQuery, Cloud Storage), or AWS (EC2, Redshift, Athena, S3);
Git for version control;
Linux/Unix experience and use of command line tools;
Exposure to data science techniques (supervised and unsupervised machine learning algorithms, time series analysis, outlier detection), ideally in a production environment;
An interest in data engineering and in working with unstructured data;
Passionate about learning new, cutting-edge technologies and finding applicable business cases as needed;
B.Sc . in applied statistics, mathematics, physics, data science, or a related discipline.
A passion for gaming.
Benefits
Lunch provided daily;
Kitchen stocked with refreshments, cereals, bread, spreads (coffee machines everywhere – our founding team is Italian after all!);
Pension plan
Flexible working environment
Monthly drinks and dinner in the office;
Monthly massages;
Quarterly team outings;
5 a side twice monthly;
Your professional growth is important to us. We provide ongoing training opportunities;

WHO WE ARE

We are Power Factors, developer of the world’s leading cloud platform for renewable energy companies. Our SaaS platform, DRIVE, is used to manage over 25 Gigawatts of renewable energy across the planet (enough to power approximately 1.5 million homes). By driving down the operations costs of wind and solar power plants, we’re tackling one of the world’s most important challenges: making renewable energy the world’s leading source of power. Our company is going through accelerated growth, fueled by the unprecedented transition to clean, renewable energy.

The DRIVE platform continues to gain traction throughout the renewable energy market. Our platform collects millions of IIoT and other data points, clean up the data, detects issues, identifies leading indicators to predict future issues, and adds full advanced analytic capabilities on top of this rich, high value dataset. In addition to issue detection and analytics, DRIVE provides the tools needed to turn analytic insight into action, such as case management and work order management.

To our clients, we deliver excellent customer service and an exceptional system of engagement that provides the results they are looking for: lower operations costs and higher output from their renewable energy power plants. We are an agile development company – big enough to make an impact, but small enough to move quickly and execute in a growing industry, taking advantage of rapidly evolving technologies. To our employees, we provide a culture that values respect, teamwork, transparency, and achievement.

THE ROLE

Power Factors is growing rapidly and is seeking an experienced Sales Executive to manage Power Factors’ direct sales, channel development, and generating revenue in the United Kingdom (UK) regions. The Vice-President, Business Development reports to the to the Senior Vice-President of Global Sales, Marketing, and Business Development.

Our UK operations are growing rapidly, and we are looking for an individual who thrives in a fast-paced environment, is entrepreneurial to the core, and gets his/her kicks from selling around the competition. The Sales Executive is responsible for stimulating sales growth by creating relationships with new customers, working with strategic partners, and devising strategies aimed at attracting target customers, and using all available sales resources to produce optimal results. Your grasp of value-added services is vital for establishing partnerships with our customers in order to better understand their needs, while providing them with a technical advisory solution.

Do you have passion for making your customers successful, and the ability to articulate the value and return on investment of an enterprise solution across multiple decision-makers? Do you have experience and relationships with the owner/operators of large renewable energy asset fleets? This could be the role for you, are you up for the challenge?

YOUR RESPONSIBILITIES

Develop and deploy market penetration strategies to ensure revenue generation;
Exceeding revenue and growth objectives;
Accurately forecasting and achieving sales targets;
Solid understanding of renewable energy industry trends, Power Factors product capabilities, and customer requirements;
Ensuring customer satisfaction;
In collaboration with Sales Engineering responsible for the development and delivery of product demonstrations, proof-of-concept, and final scoping & requirements documentation;
Responsible for representing the company and products to customers and at field events such as conferences, seminars, etc.;
Stimulating sales growth by creating relationships with new customers, devising strategies aimed at attracting target customers, and using all available sales resources to produce optimal results;
Establishing partnerships with our customers to better understand their needs, while providing them with a technical advisory solution that will be transitioned to the customer success team;
Collaborate with Strategic Partners to develop and execute sales campaigns at targeted customers.

YOUR PROFILE

Degree in Marketing, Business Administration or in a technical related discipline;
Minimum of 10 years experience in Enterprise and/or SaaS sales to renewables/power/utility industry, with an understanding of the technology/services required in Cloud/SaaS, industrial IoT, Big Data Analytics;
Significant knowledge of the Renewable Energy (wind, solar, battery) industry and related industry contacts are considered highly desirable assets;
Strong track record in achieving and exceeding sales objectives;
Experience in establishing and maintaining strong customer relationships;
Outstanding leadership with a demonstrated competency of managing technology sales through times of growth, change and ambiguity;
Experience working closely with Marketing, Sales Engineering, Product Management, and Customer Success to develop sales strategies and value-added solutions to customers deliverable over long-term SaaS contracts;
Experience in successfully managing the complete sales cycle;
Can-do attitude and hunger. You’re eager to jump in and get things done but don’t get flustered in a dynamic start-up environment;
Ability to work with cross-functional teams to help establish effective processes;
Relevant industry background and experience in Data Management, Analytics, and/or Industrials;
Share and endorse Power Factors values: delivering on commitments, mutual respect, full transparency, sustainability and environment, accountability and innovation.

REQUIRED COMPETENCIES

Business Acumen
Consultative Selling
Critical Thinking
Entrepreneurship
Influence/ Negotiation
Relationship Management
Resilience
EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER

Power Factors is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to engaging a diverse workforce and sustaining an inclusive culture. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or veteran status.

IND123

Location: East Croydon
Role: Full-time
Hours: 40 hours per week
Start Date: Immediate
COMPANY
Green Network Energy is a new independent energy and gas supplier in the UK for domestic and business customer.
The company is part of an Italian Group Green Network Spa based in Rome since 2003. Today is a top 10 Independent energy company in Europe with annual revenues of over €2billion.
As a company with big ambitions to grow, we are looking to recruit new talent to be part of our journey.
ROLE
This role offers an excellent opportunity to work in an exciting and growing energy supply company, where you will be integral part of our Customer service team! Your role will be to support the team with all data protection related queries and tasks and you will work closely with our Data Protection Adviser. Ideally, you will be a driven and engaged individual, who is motivated by challenges. You will also have a good level of knowledge of the energy industry. '
RESPONSIBILITIES
· Logging and tracking all data protection related queries;
· Conducting research and following legal and regulatory updates related to data protection- in the UK, EU and globally);
· Handling data subject requests, particularly data deletion and access requests, ensuring relevant processes are always followed.
· Supporting incident reporting and data breach investigations;
· Supporting the completion of privacy risk assessments, including data inventories; records of processing activities; privacy assessments; DPIAs;
· Keeping all data protection related documentation up to date;
Help identifying risks, requirements to improve existing practices relevant to data protection;
Supporting the delivery of data protection trainings to all staff;
Supporting the Data Protection Adviser and the CIO on data protection and information security related tasks, where required;
Supporting Customer care team with their day-to-day activities, when necessary.
*
SKILLS & EXPERIENCE
A good understanding of UK and EU Data Protection laws, in particular the Data Protection Act 2018 and the GDPR;
Relevant experience in a similar role, preferably in the energy sector;
Excellent organisational, time management and communication skills;
Eager to learn;
Able to manage and work to strict deadlines;
Excellent verbal and written skills with the ability to show attention to detail;
· Conflict resolution and strong communications skills;
Innovate, create solutions, and engage with colleagues and customers in a friendly professional way.
BENEFITS
· Competitive Salary
· Complementary hot drinks (coffee machines everywhere!)
· Game Area (table tennis and foosball table)
· Employee Preferred Tariff if you become our Customer (discounted gas and electricity bills)
· Discounts for gym
· Employee Cash Plan
GNE is a diverse and inclusive employer. We celebrate diversity. We are committed to build a team that reflects a wide variety of skills, background, and cultures. No applicant will be treated less favourably on the grounds of their sex, marital or civil partnership status, race, nationality or ethnic origin, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender reassignment, pregnancy, maternity, age, religion or belief. Applicants may be subject to a basic Disclosure and Barring Service check and at least two independent references.
Job Type: Full-time

About Behavox
We are a fast-growing and pioneering people analytics company that is transforming the financial workplace. We use cutting-edge software and machine learning to generate previously unidentifiable insights into employee behavior and performance. We have been recognized by renowned companies such as Amazon Web Services and Google Cloud for our achievements in AI, big data analytics, and machine learning. We have also been included in the Forbes FinTech 50, CB Insights AI 100, and Tech Nation's prestigious Future 50 program.
Our goal is to help businesses achieve better outcomes by developing and delivering data-driven solutions for compliance, CRM, HR, and workplace productivity. We also aim to rapidly expand our worldwide customer base to include companies across all major industries.
About the Role
Your mission will be to add more Compliance expertise to Behavox applications.
Behavox offers its clients a unique Conduct Risk Exchange (CRX), which is an online library of scenarios, reports and widgets, built by our CRX team. Our products protect Hedge Funds, Private Equity firms, Sovereign Wealth Funds, Investment Banks, and Corporations against regulatory compliance and conduct risks.
Clients trust us with compliance and reputational risks, and this trust is based on our high subject matter expertise. Now we are looking for an experienced compliance expert to add additional precision and subtlety to our applications for Behavox Data Operating Platform.
As an expert inside the CRX team, you will help to refine precision of our risk detection, add clarity and details to specifications and documentation of our compliance-related applications, enrich datasets we use to build and train models, and provide consultation to the developers working to implement the applications.
This gives you a unique opportunity: instead of observing the evil- you will be able to detect, prevent and defeat it, helping compliance controls to reach a new level and make financial and corporate worlds a safer and fairer place. You've already been a police - you'll become a superhero!
Ideal Candidate Profile
5+ years of Compliance experience
Excellent understanding of Compliance domain (Market Abuse, Code of Conduct, etc.);
Good writing skills in English;
Analytical thinking with ability to:
Dissect a risk into components;
Describe the components in a structured way;
Define, which compliance risk an example belongs to, and justify the decision;
Huge bonus: knowledge of difference between risks in different geographies: US, Europe, Asia.
Responsibilities
Sourcing (providing enforcement cases, regulations, recommendations etc. necessary for applications development);
Dataset specifications preparation (you will be responsible for text and descriptions for the true positives and false-positives expected for given policy);
Specifications development (what are the use-cases and logical components a product should cover; how to identify them etc.);
Analyse risk-related feedback and extract or explain patterns;
Provide use-cases for the risks, how they are represented in communication, what is the frequency, typical false-positives, difficulties with the identification of the issues and what information is required to tell a true positive from a false-positive for this risk; and
Internal Source of expertise for related risks: consult team members, on-boarding, work with clients during presale / implementation, etc.
What We Offer
Passionate team applying cutting-edge tech to data and analytics;
Competitive salary;
Casual dress code;
Fully covered health benefits for employee and family;
Generous time-off policy; and
Flexible work schedule.
Selection Process
HR phone interview to discuss your skills, experience, and interests;
Hiring Manager Interview
Take-home technical task assignment; and
Final on-site interview with ML Team members and Chief Data Scientist.

Elephant is a tech startup tackling the big problems in global healthcare. We create lightweight, connectable applications that improve access to care and save lives. We work in emerging economies and have partnered with NGOs, Governments, and healthcare professionals around the world.
In 2020 our platform is expanding and will reach more than 2 million new patients in Africa and the Middle East.
We are looking for a talented junior full stack engineer who can bring imagination, enthusiasm and passion to our ambitious projects.
A short video providing more information about our Kenyan operations can be found here: https://vimeo.com/369570618/a5d3d8f82f.


What sort of company are we?
We are a small band of experts. We are focused on delivering solutions to frontline professionals. Our culture is open, creative and collaborative, and we believe that products, whether used in Sudan or San Francisco should be intuitive and beautiful.
We have a culture based on security, kindness, candour, and good humour. If you think you have what it takes, please get in touch.

The role
We are looking for intermediate to senior level software developers to join our expanding development team.
Intermediate members of the team have access to exceptional senior experience across the full stack for guidance, and will be strongly encouraged to develop your their technical capabilities through self-driven learning and development.
Senior members of the team will have leadership responsibilities and ability to influence the direction of the engineering team.
Be part of a dynamic and growing engineering team specialising in creating an exceptional product firmly grounded in principles of data science and analytics.
You will be an integral part of a small and capable engineering team focused on creating exceptional products being used in some of the world’s most extreme environments.
The scope of your work includes leading and/or contributing to team sprints, assisting with technical debt, roadmapping and architecture solutions.
You will work closely with other engineers, product managers, data scientists, and designers.
We value the expertise and voice of every team member, and you will be pivotal in shaping the future of our engineering team’s culture and technical stack.
Requirements
What skills and experience would we like you to have?
Essential skills:
At least 2+ years experience working with a programming language building web/mobile apps or API services using Javascript or Python (ES or TS a bonus);
Good understanding of React. We are open to those with experience of Vue, Angular or Ember who are willing to move to React;
Experience with CSS and a templating engine (JSX great);
An appreciation of clean code and good design principles;
An understanding of algorithms and data structure;
Working with RESTful API endpoints using libraries such as Axios for request/response and parsing;
A good understanding of unit and integration testing (e.g. using Jest);
Experience with Git for version control;
An appreciation/understanding of state management in UI applications (we use Redux and RxJs);
An appreciation of working with service-based architecture (sync/async comms, CQRS etc...)
An understanding of unit, integration and acceptance testing;
Experience of, or working with relational/non-relational databases (MongoDB a plus);
Knowledge of cloud-based systems - AWS a plus;
Understanding of operating systems (Linux);
Excellent communication and organisational skills; and
Appreciation of agile methodologies, respect for testing and safe code.
Desired:
Experience building mobile apps;
Working with front-end performance problems;
Experience of writing front-end acceptance tests using Puppeteer and the headless Chrome API;
Experience of webpack;
Experience working on secure products that handle sensitive data is a major plus, e.g. Healthcare or FinTech; and
Direct experience working with ML in production.
Benefits
What do we pay and what are our benefits?
The starting pay is £45,000 pa + dependant on experience, with generous stock options for intermediate engineers. Senior engineers can expect salaries of £75,000 pa + share options dependant on experience.
Your salary and benefits will grow significantly as the company continues to grow.
We are currently working remote due to Coronavirus and hope to be able to continue to offer flexible working arrangements as we move back into an office space in central London.
Our benefits include:
Employee pension scheme with Aviva.
25 days holidays + public holidays.
We also offer the opportunity for international travel to engage with our customers on the frontline.

We are a newly-founded micromobility startup on a mission to improve European city life. We believe in a future where inner cities will be free of cars and pollution. And we believe we can make that happen by offering our dockless, shared electrical scooters and bikes as convenient alternatives for short-distance travel. Our mission is to beautifully design micromobility for safety, comfort, and durability.

We recently raised an initial investment of €20 million and just released €30 million series A funding, co-led by existing investors EQT Ventures and Naspers, through its Naspers Ventures division, Axel Springer Digital Ventures, Felix Capital, FJ Labs, U-Start Club and angel investors.

Dott is headquartered in Amsterdam and is now operating in Brussels, Paris, Lyon, Turin, Munich & soon launching in other European cities.

We’re looking for an entrepreneurial warehouse manager to develop operations team for Dott in the U.k. This is an ideal role for early career professional interested in developing real world management skills. You will report directly to the Operations Manager and will build and coordinate the warehouse team.

What you'll do:
Build your own operations team from scratch by recruiting, training and motivating team members.
Be a true leader to a large and diverse team of field technicians, mechanics (for scooters reparation) and warehouse workers/handlers;
Organise scheduling, attendance, and general administration of your operations team;
Organise and manage the flow of the workplace and optimise day-to-day activities in the warehouse;
Overseeing operations in the warehouse from facilities and vehicle upkeep to workplace safety;
Have an overview of the inventory and logistics - work with supply chain to ensure that you have the parts and tools needed to support daily operations;
Determine and track important warehouse KPI and employee performance;
Maintain accurate communication with external stakeholders and carry out final decision making processes;
Take full responsibility and ownership of projects and decisions that will impact the business.
What you'll need:
2+ years of experience in warehouse management, retail, logistics, transportation or operations management.
Have excellent communication and people skills.
Be able to justify your decisions to your team through data and measure the results.
Get your hands dirty. Work directly with your staff on the ground. Be a true leader for our warehouse team and mechanics.
Strong analytical/Excel skills a big plus.
Entrepreneurship mentality. Make decisions, learn from you experience and repeat.
Along with a competitive compensation plan, we also invite employees to participate in our employee stock option plan, plus other benefits.

Want to come along for the ride? Let’s do this right - together.

AT Internet is a global leader in digital analytics. Its Analytics Suite solution helps some of the world’s largest brands to measure, analyse and visualise their data and digital performance. A key player in an innovative and fast-growing market, AT Internet has:
More than 20,000 sites and applications measured around the world, across all industries
More than 200 enthusiastic and dynamic employees around the world (Bordeaux, Paris, London, Munich and Singapore)
20 years of experience, innovation and success in the web and digital analytics industries
AT Internet cultivates a culture of trust, customer-centricity, continuous innovation, collective intelligence, and enthusiasm within its teams.
Job Purpose
Based in London, Paddington, and reporting to the Managing Director UK & Ireland, the Account Executive’s primary role is to manage business development in UK and Ireland by creating and closing new business opportunities. By taking a consultative selling approach throughout the sales cycle, he/she will leverage internal resources, digital marketing expertise and client insight to generate leads, book meetings and lead the sales process until closing.
Key Responsibilities
Create new business opportunities and lead the sales process till closure;
Develop strategy, tactics, sales plans and profit targets;
Provide an interface between the sales function and other functional areas of the business;
Work with Pre-sales Consultant to devise the sales strategy, value proposition and joint presentation;
Provide timely and accurate commercial proposals while maintaining maximum profit margin;
Manage RFPs responses and create/lead proposal presentations;
Update job knowledge by participating in educational opportunities, reading professional publications, maintaining personal network and participating in professional membership organisations;
Manage the local partner strategy (solution partners and technology vendors);
Provide a regular reporting of pipeline, business development and other sales topics;
Work in team within the UK Office.
Skills / Qualifications
Educated to degree level (minimum BA/BSc);
3-5 years in sales / business development;
Fluent English;
A proven digital marketing experience with media customer base (broadcasters, VOD players) in the EMEA zone is a significant plus;
Knowledge of Salesforce CRM is a plus;
Strong track record of closing new business opportunities and engaging with senior stakeholders, ideally in the software industry with a SaaS business model;
Strong prospecting and negotiation skills;
Strong understanding and passion for all digital marketing channels;
Established and recognised network in Digital Analytics sector is a big plus;
Excellent communication skills – verbal, written and presentation;
Willingness to travel
Benefits
Sick paid leave
Pension Scheme
Healthcare insurance
Additional holiday entitlement based on length of employment
Giftcards
Fun events in and outside the office (afterworks, team lunches/dinners…)
Great office location in Paddington
Direct connection and communication with decision takers (board level)
One week induction program at the headquarter (Bordeaux, France)
AT Internet Summit event at the headquarter every 2 years (workshops & fun with the whole company)
International mobility possibilities among our offices around the world
Statut : Cadre
Type d'emploi : Temps plein

